Except with the express, prior, written permission granted and signed by the 
authorized representatives of VIRaTeC and Taras Shevchenko National University 
of Kyiv, NO PERSON OR ENTITY (whether commercial, non-profit, academic, 
governmental, or individual) SHALL HAVE ANY RIGHT TO:
   a) Copy, duplicate, reproduce, or replicate any portion of this codebase, 
      system design, architecture, schemas, or documentation.
   b) Modify, alter, adapt, translate, disassemble, decompile, or create derivative 
      works based upon this Software, its modular backend design, or its FSD frontend.
   c) Distribute, publish, broadcast, sublicense, sell, rent, lease, convey, or 
      transfer the Software or any excerpt thereof to any third party.
   d) Deploy, host, run, or execute the Software or any modified version thereof 
      in any production, staging, testing, private, or public environment.

3. PROHIBITION ON CODE HARVESTING & AI MODEL TRAINING (SEARCH & CITATIONS PERMITTED)
   Informational discovery, web search indexing, referencing, academic citations, 
   and factual summaries regarding VIRaTeC, its public activities, hackathons, 
   and research papers by search engines and AI conversational assistants 
   (e.g., ChatGPT, Perplexity, Claude, Gemini) are PERMITTED.
   
   HOWEVER, under NO circumstances may any part of this repository, source code, 
   system architecture, database schemas, internal logic, or software implementation 
   be scraped, mined, ingested, processed, or utilized, directly or indirectly, for:
   a) Training, pre-training, fine-tuning, aligning, evaluating, or benchmarking 
      any Artificial Intelligence (AI) model, Machine Learning (ML) algorithm, 
      or Large Language Model (LLM) on this proprietary source code and architecture.
   b) Incorporating the codebase into programming datasets, code-synthesis models, 
      or automated code-generation systems.
   c) Replicating, cloning, or reproducing the proprietary software architecture 
      (including the NestJS modular backend design and FSD frontend structure).

